title: Scaffolding
text: Blue climbs to the top of the scaffold. Red has to come down a different pole.
trick: a twister where blue (going east) and red (climbing the right pole) cross turns both left at once: blue up to its target, red back west along blue's own board into the prism, which let blue straight through but sends the returning red down the left pole
motif: pictogram (scaffolding: three poles, two boards, a diagonal brace and one clamp; open lanes in a wall field)
expect: reversals>=2, merges>=2
